{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EARLY-LAND of S1 (Gerrit change 2004 -> merged as 82190ec79b on origin/main). Rationale (skill early-land exception + regression-safety check): S1 is green on both gates (Verified +1, LLM-Review +1); it is a PURE ADDITIVE land -- mapping_config.py is imported by NOTHING yet (grep confirms only a doc-comment reference + its own def), and the _config_schema.py change only adds 'mapping' to _RESERVED_SECTIONS (exempts an unused [mapping] section from unknown-key errors). Zero change to any existing runtime path -> no regression blast radius. Landing it advances the reviewed snapshot so the dependency chain (S2..S10) plan-reviews and completion gates see mapping_config as REAL infra, instead of every dependent plan-review failing 'resolve_for_project does not exist'. Worktree reset --hard to origin/main (82190ec79b). Next: remediate S2 (438a) plan -- BLOCKED on phantom-infra (now resolved by land) + genuine gaps: outbound status translation lives in 4 consumers (jira/outbound_fields, jira/acli, jira_family/outbound_mapper, jira_datacenter/backend), rebar-status label maps hardcoded blocked/cancelled, drift-vs-applier reconciliation, drift alert provenance."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787331925728983001,"uuid":"639cf8ea-2426-4c32-b368-6058e433bfad"}